      "result": "W",
      "result_description": "May & Baker CC - 2nd XI - Won",
      "result_applied_to": "29608",
      "match_notes": "SHARMA KARMA SEES BAKER'S HOME! Baker's strolled to an easy win in this local derby. Put in to bat Rainham stuttered to 147 all out. The first 4 of the innings not coming until the 17th over, thanks to some accurate bowling from James Meecham, who again ripped through the top order to finish with 4-42 & the steady Handscombe 3-34. Extras were the top scorer with 30, until Blake came in & hit a quick 30 to give the total some respectability. John Madle had an excellent day in the field with 2 catches, & a Jonty Rhodes style run out that the umpire failed to give despite Blake being a foot short of the crease. Baker's started badly by losing James Walker for 4 in the first over of their reply. However, Shami Sharma continued his good form to smash ten fours in his 63 not out ably supported by John Wheele who was 47 not out. The two of them saw Baker's home with 9.1 overs to spare in an undefeated partnership of 143. Extras again featured with a total of 34, including 25 wides!",
